WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.175
Two facts shape where this runs.

2
00:00:02.175 --> 00:00:06.422
SQL Server needs the Azure public
cloud to use Entra authentication,

3
00:00:06.422 --> 00:00:10.740
so the design uses a commercial Azure
subscription in the same directory

4
00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:14.775
as the government tenant, and the
hosts need a path to the public cloud.

5
00:00:14.775 --> 00:00:18.930
The services it leans on are each
listed in scope for FedRAMP High,

6
00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:21.238
but a listing isn't an authorization.

7
00:00:21.238 --> 00:00:26.333
On cost, Entra authentication itself
works under a plain SQL Server license;

8
00:00:26.333 --> 00:00:31.813
the extras are Conditional Access, privileged
access management and Defender plans.

9
00:00:31.813 --> 00:00:36.291
So the authorizing official decides:
accept these leveraged services,

10
00:00:36.291 --> 00:00:40.162
after reviewing each package,
before production onboarding.

11
00:00:40.162 --> 00:00:42.213
Now, who decides what.
